        "abstract": "As this paper was presented as part of a panel discussion, it is rather brief. The purpose, however, is to illustrate the manner in which impulsive type interference such as that generated by automobiles, neon lights, electric motors, etc., in the form of arc discharges, effects double-sideband and single-sideband A.M. receivers. Also, how this interference compares with that in F.M. receivers.",
